{% import '@ModernORM/Collector/_macros.html.twig' as ui %}
<div class="morm-section-title"><h3>PostgreSQL Diagnostics</h3><span class="morm-badge">Basic · recorded request data</span></div>
<div class="morm-metrics morm-four">{{ ui.metric('SQL operations', metrics.sql.count, '', 'database') }}{{ ui.metric('Driver execution time', metrics.sql.timeMs|number_format(3), 'ms', 'clock') }}{{ ui.metric('Execution plans', null, '', 'rows') }}{{ ui.metric('Buffer / lock statistics', null, '', 'layers') }}</div>
<div class="morm-columns"><div class="morm-box"><h4>Recorded connection information</h4><dl class="morm-dl"><dt>Database system</dt><dd>PostgreSQL</dd><dt>Configured server version</dt><dd>{{ runtime.configuredServerVersion ?? 'Auto / not recorded' }}</dd><dt>SQL execution errors</dt><dd>{{ metrics.sql.errors }}</dd><dt>SQL text retained</dt><dd>{{ collector.queries|length }}</dd><dt>Bindings</dt><dd>Not collected</dd></dl></div>
<div class="morm-box"><h4>Execution-plan diagnostics</h4><p>Plans, scans, actual buffers, temporary disk usage and lock waits were not collected. No EXPLAIN or EXPLAIN ANALYZE is executed by viewing this profile.</p><p class="morm-note">Driver SQL timing is not pure PostgreSQL server execution time. The configured version is not a live server probe.</p><a class="morm-button" href="{{ profileLink }}&amp;modernorm_tab=queries">Review retained queries</a></div></div>
<div class="morm-empty"><strong>EXPLAIN integration is a separate diagnostics stage</strong><p>This panel currently uses recorded metrics only. Query replay, parameter capture and execution-plan collection require a dedicated explicit diagnostics workflow. Index or work_mem changes cannot be recommended from these counters alone.</p></div>
